WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.325
The first version rendered at 3.6 times real

2
00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:04.195
time.

3
00:00:04.195 --> 00:00:06.320
Three changes took it to 16,

4
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.725
and we'll look at the numbers for each.

5
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.625
The first version rendered at three point six

6
00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:13.058
times real time.

7
00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:15.400
Ten minutes of slides took almost three minutes

8
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.900
to export.

9
00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:19.570
Skipping unchanged frames more than doubled that,

10
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.475
to eight point three.

11
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.725
A faster x264 preset brought it to ten

12
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:26.125
point two.

13
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.350
JPEG frames finished the job at sixteen.

14
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.995
Slides spend most of their time still,

15
00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:35.483
so skipping unchanged frames gave the biggest jump.

16
00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:38.150
A frame identical to the last is reused

17
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.250
instead of captured again.

18
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.500
The x264 preset trades a little compression

19
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.045
for encoder speed.

20
00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.745
It gave the smallest gain,

21
00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:48.700
about twenty percent.

22
00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.413
JPEG frames are cheaper to produce and to

23
00:00:51.413 --> 00:00:54.525
decode than PNG, which gave another sixty

24
00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:55.458
percent.

25
00:00:55.458 --> 00:00:58.062
Together the changes make export about four and

26
00:00:58.062 --> 00:01:00.150
a half times faster.
